<title>FRANCE: Unions dislike French pension fund employer relief.</title>
<headline>Unions dislike French pension fund employer relief.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four trade unions said on Wednesday they had written to French Minister Alain Juppe to express their fears about Social Security contributions relief for employers under a legislative bill on introducing private pension funds.</p>
<p>The letter, signed by the CGT, CGC, FO and CFTC unions, was published on the eve of a Senate debate on the private pension funds bill which is likely to focus on the same issue -- relief on payroll charges for employers who contribute to the future private pensions.</p>
</text>
